# Findings reviewed and cleared, keyed by gitleaks fingerprint
# (commit:path:rule:line). This file clears ONE finding in ONE commit — unlike
# a `.gitleaks.toml` allowlist, which is a standing rule that keeps matching
# new values forever. Prefer this whenever the finding is historical and the
# working tree is already clean, so the scanner keeps its teeth on the path.
#
# A test fixture for the credential-redaction path used a realistic PKCS#8
# base64 prefix. It is the standard ASN.1 header every RSA private key starts
# with, carries no key material, and was never a credential — but its entropy
# is a key's, which is the whole point of the rule and not something gitleaks
# should be asked to tell apart. The fixture was replaced in fbbfc1d35b with a
# low-entropy marker, so the tree is clean; the finding survives only because
# the gate walks every commit in the pull request's range, and this one is now
# history.
